###   tests/provider/test_causal_question_answer.py::test_a_timing_contradiction_reads_differently and
###   tests/provider/test_direct_headline.py::test_timing_that_rules_it_out_is_the_headline_of_w18[path0-kw0] failed:
###   held-out v4 W18's repaired draft (passing on main) was rejected, "-718.24 is stated for 2026-08-19T23:05:00Z, but its
###   evidence is for another time (ev0438 2026-08-19T23:10:00Z)", on "(see the observed net interchange -718.24 MW
###   [ev0438] and the price rise from the interval ending 2026-08-19T23:05:00Z)". The time is the price rise's; clauses
###   were cut only outside brackets, so it was paired with -718.24. At 6448905 it passed only because 23:05Z is the
###   start of -718.24's 5-minute interval. Fix: "and", "while", "whereas", "but" cut clauses inside brackets too ("," and
###   ";" still only outside, where inside they list equivalents). Test: test_a_time_after_and_inside_brackets_belongs_to_
###   its_own_clause (fails with the previous rule, passes now). The probe results above are unchanged by this.
